.TH UC 1
.SH NAME
uc \- show or clean Unicode artifacts in text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uc
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ text ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uc
reads UTF-8 text and reports characters that are invisible, are format
characters, or fall outside the target encoding.
In the default mode such characters are highlighted.
.B \-s
replaces them with their code point.
.B \-c
cleans the text.
.PP
Input and output are UTF-8.
.B \-e
selects the allowed character set only, the output encoding stays UTF-8.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-show
Show problematic characters as [U+XXXX].
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-clear
Clean the output text.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-encoding " " \fIenc\fR
Target encoding: ascii, cp1252 or cp1251.
.B \-\-encoding=\fIenc\fR
works too.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit with status 1 when problems were found.
.TP
.B \-\-color=\fIwhen\fR
Colorize the output: auto, always or never.
auto is the default and colorizes only a terminal.
.SH CLEAR POLICY
.B \-c
keeps newline, carriage return, tab and ASCII printable characters.
Controls and invisible or format characters are deleted.
Unicode spaces become an ASCII space.
Typography is normalized to ASCII.
Characters outside the target encoding are folded to ASCII when a safe
approximation exists, otherwise they become a question mark.
.SH INPUT
Text arguments are processed as input strings, one line per argument.
An argument of
.B \-
reads standard input at that position.
.B \-\-
ends option parsing.
Without text arguments
.B uc
reads standard input, or prints the usage when standard input is a
terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Problems were found and
.B \-\-check
was given.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or I/O error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Highlight the invisible characters of a file:
.PP
.RS
uc < input.txt
.RE
.PP
Clean a file down to ASCII:
.PP
.RS
uc \-c \-e ascii < input.txt > output.txt
.RE
.PP
Fail on any character outside cp1251:
.PP
.RS
uc \-\-check \-e cp1251 < input.txt
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iconv (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Anastasia Shebalkina
